stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    %% ==================================================================
    %% EventFlow - REGISTRATION LIFECYCLE state machine (seats + waitlist)
    %% Matched to src/services/eventService.ts:
    %%   registerForEvent(): guards (event published, deadline open,
    %%   not ended, not already registered) -> count confirmed ->
    %%   insert "confirmed" if count < capacity else "waitlisted".
    %%   Confirmed -> generate QR ticket + confirmation notification.
    %%   Waitlisted -> waitlist notification (no ticket).
    %%   cancelRegistration(): status -> "cancelled". Only when the
    %%   cancelled status was "confirmed" a seat is freed and the FIRST
    %%   waitlisted (ordered by registered_at) is promoted to confirmed,
    %%   a ticket is generated and the DB trigger
    %%   trigger_waitlist_promotion sends the notification.
    %% NO "pending" state exists in the actual flow.
    %% ==================================================================

    classDef confirmed fill:#e6f7ee,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:1.5;
    classDef waitlisted fill:#fff8e6,stroke:#b7791f,stroke-width:1.5;
    classDef cancelled fill:#fdecea,stroke:#b91c1c,stroke-width:1.5;
    classDef note      fill:#fff9e6,stroke:#d9a441,stroke-width:1.2,stroke-dasharray:4 3;

    [*] --> Confirmed : register\n[event published, deadline open, not ended,\nnot already registered, confirmed count < capacity]\n/ insert confirmed + generate QR ticket\n+ "registration_confirmation" notification

    [*] --> Waitlisted : register\n[event published, deadline open, not ended,\nnot already registered, confirmed count >= capacity]\n/ insert waitlisted\n+ "waitlist" notification (no ticket yet)

    Waitlisted --> Confirmed : auto-promotion\n[first waitlisted by registered_at,\na confirmed seat was freed by a cancel]\n/ generate QR ticket\n+ "waitlist_promotion" (DB trigger)

    Confirmed --> Cancelled : cancel (attendee or organizer)\n/ frees one confirmed seat\n+ may trigger the promotion above

    Waitlisted --> Cancelled : cancel (attendee or organizer)\n/ no seat is freed,\nno promotion runs

    Cancelled --> [*] : terminal

    note left of [*]
      Entry guards are checked by registerForEvent
      BEFORE the capacity test: event published,
      registration deadline not passed, event not
      ended, attendee not already registered.
    end note

    note right of Confirmed
      A seat becomes available only when a
      CONFIRMED registration is cancelled;
      cancelling a waitlisted registration frees
      nothing and never promotes anyone.
    end note

    note right of Waitlisted
      No "pending" state: registerForEvent inserts
      "confirmed" or "waitlisted" directly.
    end note

    class Confirmed confirmed;
    class Waitlisted waitlisted;
    class Cancelled cancelled;